  "extractionNotes": "Father switched from employment (ended 2026-03-31) to a business on preferential contributions (0570) from 2026-04-13; while employed full time he was only health-insured from the business. Voluntary sickness insurance from 2026-04-29, the day the ZUA reached ZUS, two days after the birth (2026-04-27). ZUS insurance memo (study date 2026-06-08, reply 2026-07-02): no arrears on the study date; declared sickness base 5652.00 for 2026-04 (60% of the forecast wage) and 1441.80 for 2026-05 (30% of the minimum wage); base below 60% in 2026-05; claim form wrongly referred to code 0510. The claim is the next part of parental leave, the father's own 9 weeks, 2026-06-08..2026-08-09 (63 days); the ZUR shows a later end date in handwriting, ZUS used 2026-08-09 in the memo and the register, and a typed note says the 9-week parental benefit was granted. Earlier benefit 2026-05-25..06-07 (register title 1240) is declared on the ZUR as an earlier parental part; it may have been paternity leave. The mother declared benefit for 52 weeks from the birth and concurrent parental leave over the father's period; her periods are partly illegible and are not modelled. Rate not printed; 70% inferred for the father's own weeks. Self-employed month 2026-04 not a full insured month."
